            public/fonts/MapleMono-NF-CN-Regular.woff2 encoded from the
            official MapleMono-NF-CN-Regular.ttf. OFL text is at
            public/fonts/OFL.txt.

   Ligatures currently ON: calt, liga, clig, dlig, ss03, ss07.
   That is Maple Mono's main ASCII operator set (== != => -> && ::
   ++ // >> and [TODO]-style tags).

   Known gaps (not a full ligature enable):
   - Only Regular is shipped. Letter joins such as ff / tt / al / il
     exist on Italic only, so they do not appear in upright code.
   - ss01 ss02 ss04 are official "broken" ligature styles; leaving
     them on makes == != <= >= __ look unligatured.
   - ss06 breaks italic letter joins.
   - ss08 ss09 ss10 ss11 add extra ligatures (>>= |= /= ~=) but their
     GSUB lookups intercept equal/exclam and, in Chromium, disable
     == and !=. They stay off for that reason.
   - HTML <title>, Open Graph, Twitter, and RSS stay English.
   - Transfer size of the NF CN Regular WOFF2 is 6,296,000 bytes.
